-- pincode_geo seed — 1976 pincode centroids.
--
-- Generated from a local pincode_geo built by importPincodeGeo from the All
-- India Pincode Directory. Shipped as SQL rather than as the 165k-row source CSV
-- for three reasons: the CSV is ~20MB and does not belong in git history, the
-- estimator that turns raw post-office rows into one trustworthy coordinate is
-- expensive to re-run, and its hand-verified output is what we actually want on
-- every box.
--
-- The estimator rejects offices whose coordinates fail a plausibility gate
-- against their 3-digit prefix median, so pincodes whose offices were ALL
-- rejected are deliberately ABSENT rather than present-and-wrong. Work orders in
-- those pincodes resolve to no coordinate, which is honest; a fabricated one
-- would silently mis-rank a dispatcher's morning.
--
-- ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING: a row corrected by hand (source='manual') is never
-- overwritten by re-running this seed. That protection is the whole reason the
-- source column exists.
--
-- Idempotent. Safe to re-run.

